    13	  at submission or later, is a lost worker; the records on disk, not the pool, say which cells are saved
    14	  (`guards.reusable`). Lost cells go to `lost_cells.json` with the driver's restart estimate for 1 to 16 workers
    15	  (`restart_hours`: the lost cells' worst-case hours, longest first onto the least-loaded worker, plus 0.1 h), and the
    16	  driver exits 5; a saved round-1 mismatch outranks a lost worker (exit 4, no restart). Tests: a real worker killed with
    17	  signal 9 loses only its own cell; a sibling that dies the moment a record is on disk; one worker; a broken pool at
    18	  submission; through `main()`, exit 5 then a restart that runs only the lost cell; a mismatch with a lost worker
    19	  returns 4; the restart schedule.
    20	- Worker count: one X7-SC cell (round 1 and its evaluations, `--gate --site mac`) peaked at 2.39 GB resident on the Mac
    21	  (15 s sampling). The full three-round cell, sampled every 2 s, peaked at 3.53 GB (3534160 kB, round 3; the cell passed
    22	  all three rounds against the Mac reference; `results/pods/memprobe3/rss.log`), so `PEAKGB` = 3.54. The launcher refuses a worker
    23	  count for which workers x PEAKGB x 1.25 + 2 GB (the driver) exceeds the 28 GB minimum pod memory: 6 workers need
    24	  28.6 GB and are refused. Workers = 5; on exit 5 the launcher admits the restart with the driver's estimate for 3
    25	  workers and restarts once; a second exit 5 ends the run ("RUN FAILED ... a worker lost twice"). An early loss can leave
    26	  most cells: then the restart's admission (12.65 h for all 19 cells on 3 workers) exceeds the cap and the run stops
    27	  with the saved cells kept ("STOPPED BEFORE convergence restart"); the watchdog bounds spend, not completion.
    28	- Launcher: every directory that arrived is verified on every end state, also after a failed or partial pull of it or
    29	  of another directory (lessons.md); retried only after RUN OK. The rerun is refused until the first Run B's spend is
    30	  recorded under `convergence-` and its reservation is closed, so the follow-up total holds both runs.
    31	- Cost: run tag `convergence2`, stop cap **7 USD** (the author raised it from 5 on 2026-11-15, after the three-round
    32	  probe), watchdog bound 9.10 USD, reservation `convergence2-1` 9.10 USD. Normal run (no lost worker; three rounds for
